{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1395627-the-witcher-as-an-uratha","id":1395627,"title":"The Witcher as an Uratha","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-10T10:57:29-07:00","id":1395627,"title":"The Witcher as an Uratha","content":"Watching the TV show on Netflix and playing the game, I get a feeling that Geralt of Rivia would be a great idea for an Uratha. Here are my thoughts<br /> <br /> He is a loner hunting down monsters by himself. Probably a Storm Lord. Most Monsters look pretty hideous so they are probably monstrous Claimed.<br /> <br /> He has a silver sword just in case he needs to hunt other Uratha like himself.<br /> <br /> He has a &quot;pack&quot;, Dandelion would be a human and Yennifer would be a mage. Again, he is mostly a loner because he is a Storm Lord and does not seem to show any weakness.<br /> <br /> He utilizes the bans and banes of his prey quite extensively. <br /> <br /> It seems like a fairly good fit. He shows a great deal of restraint so he would probably stay in his human and Dalu forms the most so he could use his cunning to beat his prey rather than using his rage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T12:16:55-07:00","id":1395641,"title":"","content":"Totally, there's also the super senses. A lot of it is explained in world by alchemy and genetic alterations, but he's the 'White Wolf,' and even werewolves use alchemy and talens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T12:25:56-07:00","id":1395642,"title":"","content":"I love it!!! Or maybe a Ghost Wolf who doesn\u2019t know his heritage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T13:58:47-07:00","id":1395669,"title":"","content":"Regarding crossovers, the final episode has an excellent Mage on Mage battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-10T14:01:11-07:00","id":1395670,"title":"","content":"I would say he is a ghost wolf though. Storm Lords gather into packs as much as every other tribe. It's not admitting weakness, its smart<br /> <br /> EDIT: surprised I got a like. Thought I was being g a but pretentious there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 06-10-2020, 06:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":